# Reference transcripts built from your own recordings.
#
# No transcript file is tracked, not even a synthetic one: transcripts are the content of
# radio communications not addressed to you, and recording or republishing them is
# restricted in many countries (NL: Telecommunicatiewet art. 18.13, ITU RR 17.3). The
# format is documented in docs/user-manual.md; build your own with make_references.py.
references.txt
references-*.txt
# Timestamped backups written before any bulk correction pass -- same transcript data,
# same restriction.
references*.bak-*
identification-labels*.bak-*
identification-labels-verified.txt

# bench_identify.py ground truth, and its output. Drafted from conversations.json, so the
# note field carries transcript text and it falls under exactly the restriction above.
identification-labels*.txt
bench-identify-results*.json
# --repeats writes one of these per run set. Same reason as the line above: the per-turn
# rows carry real vessel names and MMSIs, and this repo is public.
bench-identify-repeats*.json
# Draft and scored transcript runs over replayed IQ arms -- these are verbatim recordings of
# real vessel traffic, which is the same reason the golden DSP fixtures are not committed.
# score-*.json additionally embeds the hand-verified reference for every clip.
draft-*.json
draft-*.html
score-*.json
score-*.html

# bench.py / stress.py output (generated locally; captures are user data)
bench-results*.json
bench-report*.html
stress-*.json
captures/

# bench_correct.py output. Both carry transcript text and fall under the same restriction
# as references*.txt above: the results files embed every corrected transcript per clip,
# and the cache holds each model's raw reply verbatim.
bench-correct-results*.json
bench-correct-cache/

# Secrets — never commit API keys
start-all.bat

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/

# Reference project (not part of this codebase)
WhisperPlugin/

# Few-shot examples are built from real exchanges, which are received radio traffic.
server/conversation-fewshot*.json
